      "information_risk": "high",
      "key": "rules/combat-damage",
      "lifecycle": "covered",
      "notes": "Covered for unblocked attackers and attackers blocked by one or more creatures, in two-player games of admitted lands and vanilla creatures, by the listed rules and production-endpoint cases. Damage dealt to a creature is marked on it (rules/damage-and-life). An attacker blocked by two or more creatures divides its damage among them as its controller chooses (CR 510.1c): the controller is asked, one blocker at a time, in a CombatDamageAssignment decision. First strike, trample, every other keyword and damage prevention are excluded and fail closed. No player observes blocks, combat damage to creatures or marked damage until the observation of combat is extended. No certification, card, deck, format, or playability support is claimed.",
      "owners": [
        "combat"
      ],
      "spec_path": "docs/rules/capabilities/rules/combat-damage.md",
      "summary": "One normal combat-damage step: every attacker and blocker assigns damage equal to its power, an unblocked attacker to the defending player, an attacker with one blocker to that blocker, an attacker with two or more blockers to them as its controller divides it, and a blocker to its attacker.",
      "version": "0.1.0"
    },
