      "information_risk": "high",
      "key": "rules/declare-blockers",
      "lifecycle": "covered",
      "notes": "Covered for two-player games of admitted lands and vanilla creatures by the listed rules and production-endpoint cases. A blocker whose attacker has died stays a blocking creature that blocks nothing until the end of combat (CR 509.1g). The defending player is asked, one untapped creature at a time, which attacker it blocks or no block, and any number of creatures may block one attacker, whose controller then divides its combat damage among them (rules/combat-damage). Blocking restrictions and requirements (CR 509.1b, 509.1c) and costs to block are excluded and fail closed. No player observes blocks until the observation of combat is extended. No certification, card, deck, format, or playability support is claimed.",
