      "key": "rules/state-based-actions-combat",
      "lifecycle": "covered",
      "notes": "Covered for the loss of a player at 0 or less life (CR 704.5a) and the destruction of a creature dealt lethal damage (CR 704.5g), in two-player games of admitted lands and vanilla creatures, by the listed rules and production-endpoint cases. A destroyed creature leaves combat (CR 506.4) and goes to its owner's graveyard; an attacker whose last blocker has left stays blocked (CR 509.1h), and a blocker whose attacker has left stays a blocking creature that blocks nothing (CR 509.1g). When two or more cards of one owner die together the owner orders them (CR 404.3), owners in APNAP order; when a player loses in the same batch nobody is asked, the game ends and the cards go to their graveyards in object order (owner decision 2026-10-01). Both players losing at once (CR 104.4a), a state-based action or waiting trigger in the cleanup step (CR 514.3a) and every other state-based action fail closed. Players see a death as the public zone move to the graveyard, and the order request reaches only its actor. No certification, card, deck, format, or playability support is claimed.",
      "owners": [
        "state_based_actions"
      ],
      "spec_path": "docs/rules/capabilities/rules/state-based-actions-combat.md",
      "summary": "A player at 0 or less life loses the game, and a creature dealt lethal damage is destroyed after combat damage; owners order cards that die together unless a player loses in the batch. Other state-based actions are not implemented.",
      "version": "0.1.0"
    },
